<worksheet>
  <title>Quiz: Inference for More than Two Proportions Attempt 1</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Name: <fillin characters="45"/>
    </p>

    <assemblage>
      <p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <p>
              <m>\chi^2=\sum \dfrac{(O-E)^2}{E}</m>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              <m>E_{ij}=\dfrac{(\text{row }i\text{ total})(\text{column }j\text{ total})} {\text{grand total}} \text{ where } \text{df}=(r-1)(c-1)</m>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              <m>E_i=np_i \text{ where } \text{df}=k-1</m>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              <c>data = matrix(c(1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9), nrow = 1, ncol = 1, byrow = T)</c>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              <c>chisq.test(data, correct = F)$expected</c>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              <c>chisq.test(data, correct = F)</c>
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>        
      </p>
    </assemblage>
  </introduction>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        Do men and women select different breakfasts? The breakfasts ordered by randomly selected men and women at a popular breakfast place are shown below.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        <tabular row-headers="yes" halign="center" valign="middle"
                top="medium" left="medium" bottom="medium" right="medium">
          <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
            <cell></cell>
            <cell>French Toast</cell>
            <cell>Pancakes</cell>
            <cell>Waffles</cell>
            <cell>Omelets</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Men</cell>
            <cell>93</cell>
            <cell>49</cell>
            <cell>94</cell>
            <cell>76</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Women</cell>
            <cell>112</cell>
            <cell>71</cell>
            <cell>112</cell>
            <cell>43</cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </p>
      <p>What can be concluded at the <m>\alpha = 0.01</m> significance level?</p>
      </introduction>
      <task workspace="0.1in">
        <p>What is the correct statistical test to use?</p>
      </task>
      <task workspace="1in">
        <p>Perform that test here. Include all steps of a hypothesis test</p>
      </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        In the US, 45.7% of all people have type O blood, 39.3% have type A blood, 10.8% have type B blood and 4.2% have type AB blood. A researcher wants to see if the distribution of blood type is different for millionaires. The table below shows the results of a random sample of 3120 millionaires. What can be concluded at the <m>\alpha = 0.01</m> significance level?
      </p>
      <p>
        <tabular row-headers="yes" halign="center" valign="middle"
                top="medium" left="medium" bottom="medium" right="medium">
          <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
            <cell>Blood Type</cell>
            <cell>O</cell>
            <cell>A</cell>
            <cell>B</cell>
            <cell>AB</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Frequency</cell>
            <cell>1429</cell>
            <cell>1234</cell>
            <cell>342</cell>
            <cell>115</cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace=".1in">
        <p>What is the correct statistical test to use?</p>
      </task>
      <task workspace="5in">
        <p>Perform that test here. Include all steps of a hypothesis test</p>
      </task>
  </exercise>
</worksheet>
